  "title": "Unified title",
  "summary": "FDDWAN and SPFM-Net both propose frameworks for invisible watermark removal using frequency-domain approaches, addressing the trade-off between watermark suppression and visual fidelity. These methods leverage wavelet decomposition, residual diffusion refinement, and Mamba-based architectures to enhance robustness and accuracy.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "FDDWAN introduces a Frequency-Decoupled Diffusion Watermark Attack Network (FDDWAN) that captures watermark removal through wavelet-domain decomposition and residual diffusion refinement.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SPFM-Net employs a semantic-prior-guided and frequency-constrained Mamba framework to suppress watermark-related features while preserving perceptual quality.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both FDDWAN and SPFM-Net demonstrate improved trade-offs between watermark removal effectiveness and visual fidelity compared to conventional and learning-based attack methods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
